Aim:To capture volatile memory from a live system using Dumpit and analyze memory image with volatility to extract running processes network connections arld identify hidden malicious activities

Theory:
Volatile Memory Forensics :RAM contains real-time system state including Processes, network connectens and unencrypted.
Dumpit A lightweigh windows utility that creates a fell memsry dump with minimal disk corites, preventing evidence integrity
Volatile Framework: An open-source Python based tool for analyzing memory dumps across windows Linux and macos to extract artifacts and detects malware
Malware Evasion: Attackers use process hiding, bileless bileless execution and Socket manipulation to evade traditional.
Key Artifacts: Process lists, parent-child relationships, active network connections and injected code regions revel malware

Methodology:

1. Acquisition with Dumplt.

2. Image Analysis with Volatility

  Identify Os

   List Processes

     Analysis process tree

       Extract network connections

          Detect injected code.

Future Scope)

Implement this memory forensics pipeline as an automated incident response tool that integrates with SIEM platforms to enable real-time detection, 
alerting and containment of memory-resident threats during active breaches.
